<title>USA: Protective files $200 mln preferred shelf.</title>
<headline>Protective files $200 mln preferred shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Protective Life Corp filed Tuesday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $200 million in trust originated preferred securities with a $25 liquidiation preferrence.</p>
<p>The trusts issuing the preferred will use the proceeds from the sale to purchase debt securities from parent company Protective Life.</p>
<p>Protective Life will then use the proceeds from the subordinated debt securities issued to the trusts for general corporate purposes. Merrill Lynch &amp; Co will underwrite the offering.</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
</text>
